      "writtenOn": "2024-05-30T22:50:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e That looks a big limitation and would reduce the ability to use it in real terms. What\u0027s the rationale of putting this limitation?\n\nThe `StaticItem` is a plugin public API and by definition, it\u0027s not an \"extension point\". It\u0027s a concrete API that the plugin exposes to other plugins that should not be replaced by other plugins.\n\nAs described in the first paragraph the intention here is to expose the plugin\u0027s internal state, like configuration, caches, queues, and state data. I can\u0027t imagine other plugins providing an implementation for the same purposes.\n\n\u003e I guess that it follows the DynamicItem pattern here which (if not provided) AFAICT falls back to PluginName.GERRIT - perhaps we could do the same?\n\nNo, we should not fall back to anything, what\u0027s more, I\u0027d argue that we should rather fail the startup process when the `StaticItem` is not set. This should indicate a misconfiguration, eg. the \"api.jar\" file is installed and the \"plugin.jar\" is not.\n\nThe driving use case here is the `ReplicationRemotesUpdater` which exposes configuration internal to the `replication` plugin. Since the `replication` plugin is now split into `replication-api.jar` (that binds `DynamicItem`s) and `replication.jar` (that contains plugin \"business logic\"). We need a \"bridge\" that would allow us to \"declare an interface\", that later will be bound by the main plugin JAR. In this case, we give access to other plugins to modify the `replication` plugin configuration, which is its internal state. I can\u0027t think of any valid reason why another plugin should be able to provide that implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "21a83a9a_d96d19a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "72f479f0c61d5fff4489ea4f2e8c710f4990303a",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b274bae_863d476a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
