      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-08T00:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, the `ApiModule` and the `Plugin` that provide the implementation for the `DynamicItem` are technically two different jars and have two different plugin names.\n\nI would start with a simpler approach where we just _annotate_ the `DynamicItem` to be immutable once bound and then honour that flag in `PrivateInternal_DynamicTypes.attachItems()`.\n\nWDYT @geminica.programs@gmail.com and @dariusz.luksza@gmail.com?",
      "parentUuid": "0e062b20_b9abbbba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "72f479f0c61d5fff4489ea4f2e8c710f4990303a",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16edc87d_d1826997",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1025452
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T07:09:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we perhaps have a `Provider` that gets it once so that we could just use the instance of `MyPluginApi` in the code? It is a _static_ item hence it shouldn\u0027t change and there shouldn\u0027t be a need to call `StaticItem.get()` over and over again...",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "72f479f0c61d5fff4489ea4f2e8c710f4990303a",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b43b900_46be7524",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-30T22:50:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That was my initial idea, that consumer plugins could just inject `Provider` that would either return `null` or an concrete implementation.\n\nUnfortunatley, this seems to be impossible, as we\u0027re working with `Injectors` not binders, which means that dependency resolution is already finished and we can\u0027t replace one of them.\n\nWe need that `StaticItem` wrapper, so that we can set the provider instance on it, when plugin loads, and then call that provider on `StaticItem.get`.\n\nI was contemplating, dynamic creation of child injectors for each `StaticItem` but this feels too complicated for a feature that could only be used once. We also need to remember that plugins can be loaded while Gerrit is running and re-binding everything is simply impossible then.",
      "parentUuid": "16edc87d_d1826997",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "72f479f0c61d5fff4489ea4f2e8c710f4990303a",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
