      "writtenOn": "2024-06-07T22:00:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, but also `StaticItem` doesn\u0027t tell the true story, because the association isn\u0027t static but dynamic: the implementation is bound at runtime dynamically and may not be bound at all. I still believe it makes sense to make the `DynamicItem` more intelligent rather than copy \u0026 pasting its code and renaming it.\n\nWhat we want to achieve is a `DynamicItem` that can _stick_ to the dynamic association to its first implementation.",
